Mimics in Sokoban - I hate 'em.  They always seem to mimic boulders -
why boulders?  Why not pretend to be an apple or something?  This is
especially annoying on the final "oR level, since for all the other
levels I can roughly remember where each boulder is supposed to be but
on that level everything is a complete mess and having mimics there
makes it that much worse.  These days it seems that EVERY SINGLE TIME
I do Sokoban I end up trashing my luck because of mimics.  I mean, on
regular levels you can try to push a boulder and go "Oh look, it's
atually a mimic" and kill the darn thing but in Sokoban when that last
useable boulder turns out to not be a boulder after all things can get
unbelievably hairy (scrolls of earth aren't that convenient, y'know,
especially not in those twisty little Sokoban passages).  And there's
no way to check if a boulder is actually a mimic short of going around
listening to every single one with a stethoscope, and even then you
can't check boulders you can't reach which really gets in the way of
your planning your way through the level ("Okay, so I push that
boulder down and that one to the left, and push that boulder in the
corner - oh, so that's not a boulder").

Of course, you could just read a bunch of spoilers and memorise where
every single boulder on every single level should be, but it's not
fair of the game to expect you to know that sort of thing.  I propose
that Sokoban be made a mimic-free zone, or at least the mimics should
be made so they can't mimic boulders.

